60,3,1,talk,George,,"Option A seems to address the ""asking favours"" problem. But will the distance tracking cause the ""checking figures"" resentment?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option A reduces arranging time if the calendar is respected. But recording distance is an hour a week, as the trial showed.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Option A protects my weekly trips if I book them. But I worry about the state of the car at handover.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Option A divides costs by distance. This accounts for the lopsided fuel use. But the fixed costs?,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,Option A sounds fair. But I am worried about the effort of recording every run.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,George,,"@Toshio, the hour a week is a lot. But is it less than the current arranging time?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@George, it is comparable. But it is predictable. The current arranging is unpredictable and stressful.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"Option B gives me fixed days. But if I don't use it, I still pay. And the state of the car?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"Option B is simple. But it ignores the lopsided usage. If I drive more, I pay the same.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,Option B is easy. But it feels unfair if some people drive a lot and others don't.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,George,,Option C puts the burden on one person. That person might resent the others.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,Option C reduces coordination for the others. But the keeper bears the risk and the arranging.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"Option C means I have to ask the keeper. That is the ""asking favours"" problem George mentioned.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,Option C is the most complex. The keeper has to manage everything. I do not want to be the keeper.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minato,,Option C seems hard for the keeper. I do not think it is fair to put all the work on one person.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,George,,I think Option A is the best. It addresses the favour-asking and the cost fairness. The tracking effort is manageable.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I agree. Option A reduces the unpredictable arranging time. The distance tracking is a small price.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I will vote for Option A. It protects my weekly trips and accounts for the handover state if we agree on standards.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I vote for Option A. It accounts for the lopsided fuel use and the fixed costs.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minato,,I vote for Option A. It seems the most fair and honest. I hope we can track the distance without arguing.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
